<h1>How to cite</h1>
<h2>The results</h2>
<p>Please cite the original papers. Each problem page lists them under References, with the exact statement (theorem, lemma or corollary) and the paper version each result relies on, and links to an openly readable copy.</p>
<h2>A problem page</h2>
<p>PEAR contributors, “&lt;Problem name&gt;”, <i>PEAR: Parameterized and Exact Algorithms and Reductions</i>, data of &lt;date&gt;, &lt;URL&gt;.</p>
<p class="note" style="margin-top: 8px">Each page states the date of its data at the bottom. Entry URLs are stable.</p>
<h2>Derived bounds</h2>
<p>A derived bound combines an algorithm with one or more reductions. Cite the paper of the algorithm and of every reduction in its chain (“Where this bound comes from” on the problem page), and the page itself for the combination.</p>
<h2>Data</h2>
<p>The data is released under CC0 1.0 and the code under the MIT licence. Every entry is available as JSON, linked at the bottom of each problem page.</p>
</main>
